[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777435945","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104996#issuecomment-2777435945","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104996","id":2777435945,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ljE8p","user":{"login":"KeyboardDanni","id":34800072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODAwMDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34800072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni","html_url":"https://github.com/KeyboardDanni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-04T02:51:14Z","updated_at":"2025-04-04T02:52:10Z","body":"Hmm, should we increase the default ruler size? Even at 100% editor scale it feels a bit small, especially compared to other UI elements. Granted, I'm not sure what the situation looks like on non-desktop platforms.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777435945/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2779350080","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104996#issuecomment-2779350080","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104996","id":2779350080,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lqYRA","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-04T17:28:10Z","updated_at":"2025-04-04T17:28:10Z","body":"Feels like this should be something to be handled automatically, instead, but I'm not sure how.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2779350080/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2779401918","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104996#issuecomment-2779401918","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104996","id":2779401918,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lqk6-","user":{"login":"KeyboardDanni","id":34800072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODAwMDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34800072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni","html_url":"https://github.com/KeyboardDanni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-04T17:46:56Z","updated_at":"2025-04-04T17:46:56Z","body":"Which aspect? The font size, or the ruler thickness? And do you think it should be handled based on editor scale, standard editor font size, size of the viewport, or something else? Right now it seems like it's getting the font size from the `rulers_size` font size of the editor theme, but this doesn't seem to be exposed to the user outside of custom editor themes. Weirder still, themes can't make the rulers themselves thicker or thinner, so that theme parameter more or less just controls how cramped or spacious the ruler numbers are (does this even make sense to expose on its own?). This PR currently takes that editor theme font size and multiplies it by the ruler thickness, so that the new ruler width editor setting keeps everything in sync without causing any breakage.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2779401918/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2779535272","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104996#issuecomment-2779535272","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104996","id":2779535272,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lrFeo","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-04T19:03:25Z","updated_at":"2025-04-04T19:04:46Z","body":"What you can do is read the editor font size _after_ `EDSCALE` is applied, and make it always a minimum of 10 or so (regardless of `EDSCALE`). This should ensure the ruler text is always reasonably sized regardless of editor scale or font size editor settings.\r\n\r\nWe can also increase the ruler font size by 1 unit – it should already look better at 90% editor scale this way. You can also make it so the size is always rounded up with `ceil()` instead of `round()`. Godot currently doesn't support floating-point font sizes, so some kind of rounding has to happen either way.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2779535272/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781526689","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104996#issuecomment-2781526689","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104996","id":2781526689,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lyrqh","user":{"login":"KeyboardDanni","id":34800072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODAwMDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34800072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni","html_url":"https://github.com/KeyboardDanni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-06T17:37:35Z","updated_at":"2025-04-06T17:39:20Z","body":"So here's my thinking:\r\n\r\n- We want a decently legible ruler font out of the box without configuration.\r\n- But we should still allow the user to tweak this (within reason) if the size isn't quite right.\r\n- The ruler font is technically legible at 100% editor scale (though smaller than most UI elements which feels a bit weird to me).\r\n- At 90% editor scale, the ruler font is too small to read comfortably.\r\n- The font size is currently set by the editor theme but the ruler width itself is not customizable the same way.\r\n- If we increase the font size too much without increasing the ruler, it will look cramped or possibly overflow the ruler.\r\n- We can probably afford to increase the ruler's size by a little bit. Especially since there are other elements taking more space, and if the user can comfortably use Godot at 100% editor scale, they likely have a few pixels to spare.\r\n- Currently the ruler numbers overlap the ticks. #104993 has a fix.\r\n\r\nSo I'll probably make the following changes to this PR:\r\n\r\n- Wait for the above PR to be merged, then rebase on top of it.\r\n- Slightly increase default editor theme ruler font size.\r\n- Increase default ruler width by a few pixels.\r\n- Clamp the font size so the numbers are at least 7px tall (after scaling is applied?) but still have at least 2 pixels of space from the top edge and bottom ticks.\r\n\r\nThough I'm not sure what to do if the ruler width doesn't give enough space for at least 7px of font. Do we force-shrink the font to avoid overflow, or force-grow the ruler width? And does it even make sense to allow the user to drop the ruler width to 12? That's three steps below the default of 15 which is already quite small on the lower editor scales.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781526689/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2784058325","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104996#issuecomment-2784058325","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104996","id":2784058325,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6l8VvV","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-07T17:19:53Z","updated_at":"2025-04-07T17:19:53Z","body":"> Though I'm not sure what to do if the ruler width doesn't give enough space for at least 7px of font. Do we force-shrink the font to avoid overflow, or force-grow the ruler width? And does it even make sense to allow the user to drop the ruler width to 12? That's three steps below the default of 15 which is already quite small on the lower editor scales.\r\n\r\nI would either force-grow the ruler width, or hide the ruler text entirely. There isn't an ideal solution here, but I would avoid displaying text that will never be readable.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2784058325/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2784128927","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104996#issuecomment-2784128927","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104996","id":2784128927,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6l8m-f","user":{"login":"KeyboardDanni","id":34800072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODAwMDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34800072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni","html_url":"https://github.com/KeyboardDanni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-07T17:52:51Z","updated_at":"2025-04-07T17:52:51Z","body":"I'll probably go with growing the ruler. Removing the ruler numbers would make the ruler mostly useless. That could be counteracted with showing a number label on mouse hover, but that wouldn't be a good experience for touch-based input.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2784128927/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2787454046","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104996#issuecomment-2787454046","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104996","id":2787454046,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mJSxe","user":{"login":"KeyboardDanni","id":34800072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODAwMDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34800072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni","html_url":"https://github.com/KeyboardDanni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-08T19:23:14Z","updated_at":"2025-04-08T19:23:14Z","body":"Changelog:\r\n\r\n- Rebased on top of #104993.\r\n- Ruler font size now has a minimum cap of 8px after scaling (meaning you're less likely to hit it at higher editor scales).\r\n- Ruler will enlarge to comfortably hold the ruler font size. In practice this shouldn't have much visible effect if any, unless we hit the minimum ruler font size.\r\n- Increased default ruler width from 15 to 16.\r\n- Tweaked the tick frequency so it properly follows the editor scale to avoid overcrowding.\r\n- Ruler number horizontal offset also follows the editor/ruler scale now, giving the tick labels some room to breathe at higher scales.\r\n\r\nI'm pretty happy with how it looks now. I think it even makes some improvements in other areas besides just having the font big enough to read. Spacing is also much nicer IMO.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2787454046/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"p